# Moxa ioLogik E1242.
# Converted automatically from the Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST); see ATTRIBUTION.md.
# Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation.
# Corrections are welcome (CONTRIBUTING.md). Remove @x_status once this table has been checked against the manual.
# | Moxa ioLogik E1242 Remote Ethernet I/O — 4 AIs + 4 DIs + 4 DIOs
# | 
# | Source: ioLogik E1200 Series User Manual V16.2, August 2025 (Appendix A)
# | Protocol: Modbus/TCP (port 502); Modbus/TCP ID default = 1
# | NOTE: AI_scaledValue incorporates word swapping; DI_counterValue incorporates byte swapping.
# | 
# | AI channels (ch0-3):
# | FC04 addr 512-515: AI_rawValue (word, R)
# | FC04 addr 520-527 (2 words/ch): AI_scaledValue hi/lo (u32, R) [word swapped]
# | FC04 addr 528-531: AI_rawValueMin (word, R)
# | FC04 addr 532-535: AI_rawValueMax (word, R)
# | FC04 addr 536-543 (2 words/ch): AI_scaledValueMin hi/lo (u32, R)
# | FC04 addr 546-553 (2 words/ch): AI_scaledValueMax hi/lo (u32, R)
# | FC04 addr 576-579: AI_status (word, R; 0=normal,1=burnout,2=over range,3=under range)
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Moxa
@model=ioLogik E1242
@description=4-AI + 4-DI + 4-DIO remote Ethernet I/O, Modbus/TCP. AI FC04: AI_rawValue (512-515), AI_scaledValue u32 word-swapped (520-527), AI_rawValueMin (528-531), AI_rawValueMax (532-535), AI_scaledValueMin (536-543), AI_scaledValueMax (546-553), AI_status (576-579). AI FC03: AI_mode ch0-3 (544-547), AI_burnoutValue u32 ch0-3 (560-567). DI FC02: DI_status (0-7), DI_counterOverflowFlag (1000-1007). DI FC04: DI_counterValue byte-swapped u32 (16-31). DO FC01: DO_status (0-3), DO_pulseStatus (16-19). DO FC03: DO_all_status (32), DO_pulseCount ch0-3 (36-39), DO_pulseOnWidth unit 1ms (52-55), DO_pulseOffWidth unit 1ms (68-71).
@source=Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/moxa-iologik-e1242.toml; Source: ioLogik E1200 Series User Manual V16.2, August 2025 (Appendix A). Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation
@byte_order=ABCD
@address_base=0
@x_status=unverified
@x_origin=omniconsole

